                    "name": "END-S5-LAB",
                    "label": "Safety - laboratory evaluations",
                    "text": "Laboratory evaluations: haematology and chemistry parameters, analysed as change from baseline and as shifts in reference-range indicator. Baseline is the last non-missing value on or before first dose (SAP section 12.3).",
                    "description": "The protocol names Safety as a key secondary endpoint and section 7.2 schedules laboratory assessments. The SAP does NOT define a laboratory analysis: ADLB appears only in the data-handling conventions (sections 12.2, 12.3 and 7), and the three safety estimands in section 13.7 are all adverse-event based. This endpoint is therefore authored from the protocol, not from the SAP, and that gap is recorded as discrepancy D11.",
